{"assets":["/statement-assets/e27e3eb67b400e543d76e7540a8ff2e474a3e632fa1bc896a941949877452ca8.png","/statement-assets/e1b79a19f8aa111f9a8e83ee1e199e653ec69ff1d145c2a944018a274ca0560e.png","/statement-assets/8a0bfb55f4a42c0fc414dd405bcd48cae9da65b19536890356e896839a8efacd.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1624","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. MinOr Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recently, Vlad has been carried away by spanning trees, so his friends, without hesitation, gave him a connected weighted undirected graph of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$m$$$ edges for his birthday."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vlad defined the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ority"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a spanning tree as the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://tiny.cc/bitwise_or"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of all its weights, and now he is interested in what is the minimum possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ority"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" that can be achieved by choosing a certain spanning tree. A spanning tree is a connected subgraph of a given graph that does not contain cycles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In other words, you want to keep $$$n-1$$$ edges so that the graph remains connected and the bitwise OR weights of the edges are as small as possible. You have to find the minimum bitwise OR itself."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An empty line is written in front of each test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is followed by two numbers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5, n - 1 \\le m \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of vertices and edges of the graph, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$m$$$ lines contain the description of the edges. Line $$$i$$$ contains three numbers $$$v_i$$$, $$$u_i$$$ and $$$w_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le v_i, u_i \\le n$$$, $$$1 \\le w_i \\le 10^9$$$, $$$v_i \\neq u_i$$$) — the vertices that the edge connects and its weight."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum $$$m$$$ and the sum $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$ and each test case contains a connected graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$t$$$ lines, each of which contains the answer to the corresponding set of input data — the minimum possible spanning tree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ority"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n\n3 3\n1 2 1\n2 3 2\n1 3 2\n\n5 7\n4 2 7\n2 5 8\n3 4 2\n3 2 1\n2 4 2\n4 1 2\n1 2 2\n\n3 4\n1 2 1\n2 3 2\n1 3 3\n3 1 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n10\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e27e3eb67b400e543d76e7540a8ff2e474a3e632fa1bc896a941949877452ca8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Graph from the first test case."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e1b79a19f8aa111f9a8e83ee1e199e653ec69ff1d145c2a944018a274ca0560e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ority"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of this tree equals to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 or 2 = 2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and it's minimal."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8a0bfb55f4a42c0fc414dd405bcd48cae9da65b19536890356e896839a8efacd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Without excluding edge with weight $$$1$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ority"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 or 2 = 3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1624G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1624/problem/G"}